	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The paper states, “Missing clinical data was median imputed,” which is simple imputation. The cohort was split “75%:12.5%:12.5% train:test:validation,” so for 160 patients this corresponds to about 120 training and 20 held-out test patients. Preprocessing included DICOM handling, grayscale normalization, automatic exclusion of the top 15% and bottom 5% of scan series, resizing/cropping, and feature ablation. Class imbalance was addressed using focal loss optimized for AUPRC. Code availability was not reported in the retrieved text.  ￼

